      "writtenOn": "2017-02-23T00:13:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fair question.\n\nFakeProcess doesn\u0027t inherit any functionality from (real) Process. I just think this approach is easier to read than the alternative.\n\nIn more detail:\n- Given that we don\u0027t verify any interactions with |mExternalProcess|, we don\u0027t need a mock. We just need a stub or a fake. (go/tott-296)\n- We can create a stub using Mockito, or we can explicitly write a fake.\n- If we use Mockito, then, in the context of setUp(), we have to understand the intent of all the thenReturn() calls. That is, what are all the thenReturn()s trying to accomplish?\n- With an explicitly written fake, we can separate the intent from the implementation details. In setUp() we just need to know that we\u0027re using a fake. Only when we\u0027re reading FakeProcess code do we need to understand the implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "fdef3a66_ada5f8ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 809,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 809,
        "endChar": 45
      },
